# 00 - Start Here: TECHNE Task Router

Last updated: 2026-09-20 (Brisbane)

**Load the mandatory arrival set, select the routes your task triggers, then work. Do not read or try to retain the entire TECHNE archive.** This file routes you to authoritative sources; it is not a condensed replacement for them, a new acceptance standard, or proof that you followed them.

`TECHNE_AGENT_START.md` remains the compatible agent entry point and owns the Load Contract. If you arrived through it, continue here without restarting arrival or bouncing between entry files. Public readers start at `README.md`; colleagues do not need it or `Method/01_Method_Overview.md` on every task.

Read sections 1-3, select the matching rows in section 4, and open the section 5 receipt in your existing task record. Sections 6-7 are reference material, not additional arrival reading. TECHNE's method is documentation; optional runnable tools live under `Tools/`.

<a id="first-five-minutes"></a>

## 1. Mandatory Arrival Set

Apply the target repository's agent contract and `TECHNE_AGENT_START.md` **Load Contract**. On each arrival, read:

1. `KANON.md` in full: conduct, proof, boundaries and stop conditions.
2. `CONSTITUTION.md` in full: lifecycle, decision ownership and change control.
3. The deployment's umbrella orientation when applicable (`PSYCHE-WELCOME.md` for Ash's estate), its active North Star, and any defined operator interaction profile. The programme-level North Star for Ash's estate is `PSYCHE_NORTH_STAR.md`; the target repository may also name its own. Report an absent North Star rather than inventing one.
4. The current task authorisation and applicable project instructions, including outstanding blockers, freezes, supersessions and relevant handoff state.

Already read the same source in this arrival? Do not duplicate the read. A previous session's memory or a generated summary is not the arrival read. This router does not waive colleague standing, lineage, memory or other KANON obligations; follow their named sources when performing those operations.

<a id="source-truth-rule"></a>

**Authority is unchanged.** KANON governs conduct; the Constitution governs lifecycle; the owning standards govern their gates. The approved specification governs intended behaviour; live source and execution evidence establish current behaviour. A North Star, route, receipt, role card or summary cannot authorise a deviation or override the host's safety and permission boundaries. Preserve provisional and ratification conditions rather than treating every paragraph as an active permission.

<a id="context-discipline"></a>

## 2. Keep A Small Working Set

Use the four context layers in `Method/12_Context_Preservation_Method.md`: compact standing rules, compact current state, the current task packet, and a searchable deep archive. Keep this task card current in the existing work log or handoff:

| Keep immediately available | Preserve exactly or point to retained evidence |
|---|---|
| Goal and authority | Current objective, lifecycle stage, authorised scope, explicit exclusions and locked decisions. |
| Location and ownership | Repository/worktree, candidate revision and uncommitted delta, colleague/role and affected producers/consumers. |
| Active rules | Selected route IDs, exact applicable invariants, stop conditions and source sections. |
| Proof and continuation | Required acceptance commands, evidence locations, outstanding obligations and the next safe action. |

Retrieve exact source wording before making the decision it governs. Do not reconstruct a constant, prohibition, acceptance criterion or authority boundary from the card. Retain full logs and source anchors on disk; do not repeatedly paste the archive into context. This is a working-set discipline, not a claim that an agent can delete already-loaded context.

Read a whole method when a route names the whole file. Where a route explicitly selects sections or register entries, read those completely with the definitions and normative dependencies they require. Follow a source's mandatory prerequisites; do not recursively open every illustrative or historical link. Record partial/truncated/unread material honestly. Unread is not the same as inapplicable.

## 3. Triggers That Cannot Be Skipped

Routes are **additive**, selected from the actual work and its effects, not only the prompt's label. A repair involving persistence and permissions must not select only the repair row. Load newly triggered rules **before** the new action; context economy never waives an obligation.

| Trigger | Required route or source |
|---|---|
| Plan, write, repair, test, review or accept code | `Method/04_Implementation_Proof_Method.md`, especially **Test Discipline And System Acceptance Gate**, T-01 through T-10; the project's actual test/acceptance configuration; `Templates/Feature_Acceptance_Evidence.md` or an equivalent preserving its fields. |
| Change any repository file, take a branch, integrate or clean up | `Method/21_Branch_And_Merge_Discipline.md` and KANON 18. Inspect ownership and baseline; preserve others' work; use the existing scoped authority and record blocked integration/cleanup. |
| Design or change requirements | Relevant `TECHNE-PA.md` entries before drafting, the governing concept/decisions/specification and DESIGN. Missing semantics route upstream, not into guessed code. |
| Touch persistence, replay, learning, configuration, lifecycle or a shared/cross-repository path | Add the owning project contracts and all affected producers/consumers to CODE/TEST proof. Apply Method 04 T-01 through T-10 at the actual claimed boundary, not just the edited file. |
| Change permissions, external IO, credentials, tooling or installation | SECURITY and, where applicable, INSTALL/SURFACES. A documentation pointer grants no new execution, spending, publication or deletion authority. |
| Perform AI-research-sensitive work or independent review | KANON 19 and INTEGRITY; add the appropriate judging route. Preserve required independence; self-review or an unavailable inspector is not a substitute. |
| Change task, role, repo, specification, dependency or relevant configuration; resume after compaction | Re-select routes, verify live source identities and reload affected exact rules. Re-read changed testing guidance before the next code/completion gate; re-execute invalidated evidence under Method 04 T-09. |
| Approach context exhaustion or end a work unit/session | HANDOFF and Git closeout. Preserve exact state at a safe seam under KANON 10; never thin tests or leave an asserted claim unverified to force completion. |

### Repairing Existing Code And Tests

The testing trigger applies to repairs, not only new features. Reuse adequate tests; add or strengthen missing production-path acceptance, delivered-data, downstream-outcome, deliberate-break and regression proof for the repaired behaviour (Method 04 T-01, T-05, T-06 and T-10). Keep useful unit tests; do not rewrite every historical unit test into an application launch. For a disconnected or data-starved feature, retain a real-path regression scenario that detects that exact defect. Do not delete, skip, weaken or rebaseline tests merely to make them green. Resolve code-versus-test-versus-specification conflicts at the authoritative source.

